  "interpretation": "The corrected release kept 2,008,410 of 2,099,976 rows under the strict policy (21.2030% positive). On the grouped test partition the portable model reached ROC-AUC 0.9988 and average precision 0.9916. The original-Kaggle P3B arm reached ROC-AUC 0.9859 and average precision 0.9297 under the same split algorithm; the corrected-arm deltas are +0.0129 and +0.0618. Test prevalence was 19.0942% in the original arm and 21.2914% in the corrected arm; average precision is prevalence-sensitive, so the AP comparison needs that context. The validation-selected threshold saturated at 1.000000 for 10_per_10k, 100_per_10k; strict test alerts are therefore zero by construction, not a measured false-positive rate. Because the corrected release is also a CICFlowMeter re-extraction, a difference cannot be attributed to labels alone. This is a sensitivity check, not a replacement for the original result and not external evidence.",
  "limits": [
    "The corrected release is both a relabelling and a re-extraction with a fixed CICFlowMeter. A difference from the original Kaggle arm cannot be attributed to labels alone.",
    "The strict policy excludes every `- Attempted` row. That is a policy choice, not evidence that attempted attacks are harmless.",
    "This is an in-distribution sensitivity under the P3B stratified-group protocol. It does not report external transfer and does not establish deployability.",
    "The serving artifact, the frozen Tier A schema, and every existing claim are unchanged."
  ]
